Lots is being written since the yen intervention and the QRA language change.  The idea is that the treasury is going to protect the long term bond market (suppress interest rates).  That has direct consequences to currency markets.  Over a year ago I described it as a choice between protecting spot money or future money.  Here's the choices.  BUT without dealing with the root problems eventually like in Japan you cannot protect either form of money.

For one I strongly disagree with the idea that the language change was a signal that coupon Auctions would decrease going forward.  I think it was a useful change because one day a particular bond like the 20 year may actually decrease.  BUt in aggregate there is almost no chance that coupon auctions can decrease in total.  So I think it's a wild goose chase idea from those wanting to pump gold and stocks and not a serious change. BUT if they do in fact reduce coupon auctions in November or any time in 2027 it's giving up on the USD and I could see DXY in the 80's soon after.

